{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[operator-attested] EVIDENCE for AC4 and AC5. These two criteria are attested because their\nproof is a local execution record, not a repository artifact.\n\nLANDED: Gerrit change 1676, \"Stop fixture remote rewriting itself mid-push\", status MERGED\nwith LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. The Verified vote is CI's own execution of `make lint`,\n`make typecheck` and the full suite against this patchset, so AC5 additionally has an\nindependent external witness beyond the local run below. Note for the record: patchset 1\ntook a Verified -1 that was NOT this change — the complexity-baseline lock reported a new\nentry for `dispatch_one.py::_update_one_dispatch_links`, a function this test-only change\ndoes not touch, introduced when main advanced. A rebase onto current main cleared it\n(`check_complexity_baseline.py --check` then reported `active=60 new=0 increased=0\nstale=0`). An earlier lint-job failure on the same patchset was an infrastructure flake: ruff\ncheck and ruff format --check both passed, then the actionlint binary download returned HTTP\n503 four times.\n\nAC4 — command actually run, 20 iterations, each on a fresh basetemp that is deleted\nafterwards, with `git fsck` run over every `remote.git` the iteration produced:\n\n    for i in $(seq 1 20); do\n      bt=/tmp/flakebase/run$i; rm -rf \"$bt\"\n      python -m pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py \\\n        -n 4 --dist loadgroup -q --timeout=300 --basetemp=\"$bt\"\n      for r in $(find \"$bt\" -name remote.git -maxdepth 4); do\n        git --git-dir=\"$r\" fsck --no-progress || echo \"CORRUPT $r\"\n      done\n    done\n\nResult, one line per iteration, all 20 identical in shape:\n\n    iter 1  rc=0 corruptremotes:none  31 passed in 35.36s\n    …\n    iter 20 rc=0 corruptremotes:none  31 passed in 34.24s\n    TOTAL FAILS: 0 / 20\n\n620 test executions, zero failures, and `git fsck` clean on every remote produced. Worth\nrecording because it shows the harness measured what it claims: an earlier run of the same\nloop returned `TOTAL FAILS: 1 / 20`, and the single non-zero exit was the suite's own\nrepo-isolation guard reporting `REPO ISOLATION FAILURE … M tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/\norchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` — an unrelated file this session was editing at the time\n— with all 31 tests passing. Re-run against a clean tree, it was 0/20.\n\nAC5 — `make lint` (ruff check, ruff format --check, complexity baseline, DCO identity,\ncriteria vocabulary, skill frontmatter, zizmor, actionlint) and `make typecheck` (mypy) both\npass locally on the committed tree:\n\n    ruff check src tests scripts        -> All checks passed!\n    ruff format --check src tests scripts -> 1929 files already formatted\n    check_complexity_baseline --check   -> active=60 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n    mypy src/rebar scripts              -> Success: no issues found in 511 source files\n\nSuite: the affected file passes (31 passed) and the reconciler unit tree passes (2409\npassed). `make config-check` and `pre-commit run --all-files` also pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786570602101412001,"uuid":"70e85190-6c56-453a-837a-fc14c47d6dd1"}